<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Tesla is a 46-year-old electrical engineer in treatment for obsessive-compulsive disorder with exposure and response prevention and sertraline 150 mg, who asked for a same-day visit. Thirty-six hours ago he began vomiting, followed by watery diarrhea about six times a day, cramping, and aching. Two engineers on his staff had the same illness last week. He vomited four times yesterday and not since this morning, and he is keeping down small sips of water. He has had no blood in the stool, severe abdominal pain, or high fever. He vomited his sertraline yesterday morning and has not taken it since. The illness has stirred his contamination fears: he has been washing his hands more than he has for months and has wiped down his apartment twice. He is upset that this undoes his progress. He has had no suicidal thoughts. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Vomiting 36 hours ago, then watery diarrhea about six times a day</td></tr><tr><td>Exposure</td><td>Two colleagues had the same illness last week</td></tr><tr><td>Red flags</td><td>No blood in the stool, severe pain, or high fever</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Sertraline 150 mg vomited yesterday; none taken since</td></tr><tr><td>OCD</td><td>Washing and cleaning increased with the illness</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>No suicidal thoughts</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
